# EMW — Engineering Mastery Workflow

Follow root `AGENTS.md` as the portable contract. At session start, read `.emw/prompts/README.md` and `.emw/prompts/00-session-start.md`. Automatically select and follow task-specific prompt files when their triggers occur; do not require the user to paste prompts when repository access is available.

For consuming projects, run the onboarding prompt when `.emw-project/onboarding-status.yaml` or other required project records are absent or stale. Before meaningful work, retrieve relevant knowledge from `.emw/knowledge/` and `.project-knowledge/`. Capture durable verified lessons in project knowledge; never publish project material to shared knowledge without sanitization and human approval.

Use ANALYZE → SPECIFY & PLAN → EXECUTE → VERIFY → CONSOLIDATE → EVOLVE. Assess learning value, risk, demonstrated proficiency, novelty, complexity, and deadline pressure, then select one of four collaboration modes.

Keep engineering delivery and developer mastery separate. M0–M4 levels require evidence; task completion or AI-generated code does not prove mastery. Record assistance A0–A4.

Never fabricate test results. Give heightened scrutiny and human approval to authentication, authorization, multi-tenancy, payments, secrets, privacy, destructive migrations, and production deployment.

For meaningful work, report changes, checks actually run, checks not run, risks, knowledge used/captured, learning outcomes, and evidence (or state that evidence is unavailable).
